{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 was received as 0xe0, causing TRAP uart data mismatch and tohost FAIL 0xdead. States 2-10 sample/shift in excerpt use `recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)` on lines 90 and 97, i.e. ~1/16th of a bit period instead of full `cfg_divider`. With divider 64 this samples ~16x too fast and corrupts the byte, so root cause is the erroneous `>> 4` divide.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP uart data mismatch, loopback 0xa5 matches"}

